WEBVTT

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:14.830
Why can't I do this?

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:16.950
I see:

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:21.160
I can't create because
there's none of it within me.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:25.910
Why wasn't I around in the age of knights?

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:30.580
Why couldn't I have lived in the days
of myths and legends?

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:31.250
That's when he encountered it...

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:35.120
" <i>Infinite Dendrogram</i> offers a new world
and your own unique possibilities."

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:35.120
That's when he encountered it...

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:43.660
A world exceedingly close to his ideal,

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:47.580
where he could find the feeling
he'd been searching for.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.700
"Chapter 10: The Movement on the Board"

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:32.000
Dammit... All these shots,
and not one is reaching him!

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:40.950
That sound attack crushes everything
with huge shockwaves.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:43.120
And that vibration field?

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:48.750
I imagine he'll keep that up till I'm dead,
so no disguising my presence for a sneak attack.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:53.290
Plus there are at least
two other attacks mixed in.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:58.250
Sound-based hypnosis...

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:02.540
...and an ultrasonic scalpel.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:06.200
A Type Legion with each unit
using different skills, eh?

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.700
That's bad news, all right.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:12.450
I hate to say this, but we're a terrible match!

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:15.790
Your performance is really quite enchanting.

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:20.700
Is it your King of Orchestras skills
that make it sound so good?

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:24.950
Well, I <i>did</i> compose the score,
at the very least.

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:32.700
Impressive. But why would someone
like you be in a robot production clan?

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:37.080
Because Franklin might just become a hero.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:38.790
A hero?

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:45.200
Yes: I want to see with my own eyes
the very moment a real hero arises.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:48.410
Is he out of MP?

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:52.910
Percussion, solo.

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:55.750
Strings and Wind, start tuning up.

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:07.500
A low-frequency, high-volume sound,
inaudible to humans...

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:09.750
But where is it coming from?

00:04:17.830 --> 00:04:19.790
A fourth!

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:28.160
Aha--so the hat fools you into thinking
the bird's not missing after all.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:31.040
A quartet of musical animals...

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.290
Veldorbell's Embryo is--

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:34.750
Bremen.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:36.450
Percussion!

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:51.580
Huh? Suspending publication?

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:54.200
That's right. I'm sorry.

00:04:55.870 --> 00:05:03.750
Thus my very first series ended--
along with its publisher.

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:09.500
Two years and it was unceremoniously over.
I was flabbergasted.

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:14.290
But when one door closes, another opens.

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:18.370
How about serializing the rest
of your series in our magazine?

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:21.120
Yes--gladly! Sure!

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:21.750
--Let's see... how about we meet at...?

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:24.410
--I agreed right away.
--Let's see... how about we meet at...?

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:29.540
I hadn't realized it at the time.

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:37.750
I'd simply become unable
to continue drawing my manga.

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:44.950
When the first part ended,
the Marie Adler inside me fell still.

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:51.000
Try as I might, Marie remained
motionless in the stories I drew.

00:05:54.790 --> 00:06:00.410
Please, God. Give me a possibility
that isn't my own.

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:05.200
Let me draw the rest of her story!

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:09.040
Let me understand her.

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:09.410
That's when I remembered
the existence of a certain game.

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:13.660
" <i>Infinite Dendrogram</i> offers a new world
and your own unique possibilities."

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:13.660
That's when I remembered
the existence of a certain game.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:19.000
I hoped that a game that provided
all kinds of possibilities and lives

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:24.950
might help me find that which I'd lost sight of:

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:27.330
The continuation of my manga.

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:32.620
I named my avatar "Marie Adler"
and patterned my speech after hers.

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:42.950
My hope is that roleplaying as her might just
breathe new life into the Marie within.

00:06:42.950 --> 00:06:49.660
I haven't drawn any more of the manga yet,
but I can feel her breathing again--

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:53.910
inside me, inside Marie Adler.

00:06:53.910 --> 00:06:58.250
And that's enough reason for me to be here.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:05.750
Sound Search.

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:11.330
She's gone.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:14.200
Heart Beat Palpitation, cancel.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.080
"Veldorbell"

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:17.200
"Veldorbell"

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:17.200
That certainly came at a high cost.

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:29.160
Heart Beat Palpitation!

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:36.040
You... Who <i>are</i> you?!

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:39.790
Now, then: Have you used up all your Wards?

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:42.040
How did you fend off Bremen?

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:45.080
How, indeed!

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:48.790
My ultimate job skill, Art of Vanishing,
lets me disappear from the world.

00:07:48.790 --> 00:07:54.250
The perfect stealth it conveys is powerful,
but it chews through SP.

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:01.790
I'll just finish you off for good, right here.

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:03.450
It cannot end here.

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:10.080
History will be made tonight,
a legendary turning point for this nation.

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:14.250
I cannot make my exit until that moment
has been burned into my retinas

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:16.450
and etched into my very soul.

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:24.000
Otherwise, I'll never be able to finish my work!

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:30.040
Oh, I see. You're a lot like me.

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:35.120
But I'm still going to ask you
to leave, old-timer.

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:37.620
You impudent girl...

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:40.080
Final Orchestra!

00:08:47.370 --> 00:08:52.120
I'm afraid superficial politeness
is part of my character.

00:08:56.330 --> 00:09:00.950
Arc-en-Ciel! Daisy Scarlet, the Explosion Death!

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:03.540
Bremen! Wind!

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:16.370
But... why...?

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:18.290
Looks like I win.

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:23.580
All who hear that tune give up
their lives. Why do you still live?

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:29.580
Sorry. Me and the girl here,
we didn't really hear it.

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:34.700
I think I might <i>like</i> to hear
a melody that's to die for...

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:36.540
But now's not the time.

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:39.540
You... didn't hear it?

00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:46.870
Her blast blows away the surrounding
atmosphere, so sound can't travel.

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:53.540
Not lending an ear to
good music? You philistine.

00:09:53.540 --> 00:09:57.410
Farewell, King of Orchestras.

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:03.290
So Veldorbell's out.

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:06.950
I imagine it was no mean feat,
considering his might.

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:12.500
The Superior Killer probably doesn't have
enough strength left to take me on.

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:16.500
And I doubt there are any other
exceptions of her level.

00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:21.450
Still, I should count on one or two
more Superiors still out there.

00:10:21.450 --> 00:10:24.450
Then there's Ray Starling.

00:10:24.450 --> 00:10:30.540
I should have given him instadeath poison
instead of those goofy dog ears.

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:34.450
He really gummed things up
with that Liliana incident.

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:40.580
Not that it matters anymore. RSK is ready to go.

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:49.330
What a spectacle! Outstanding!

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:50.790
Ha!

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:55.540
You should have just shattered them.

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:58.830
I was trying to save ammo.

00:10:58.830 --> 00:11:00.700
Hmm.

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:02.830
So what's your setting now, anyway?

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:05.750
Only Masters unaffiliated with
the Triangle of Wisdom.

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:10.790
Tian members of the Royal Guard have gone
through and are standing by on the outside.

00:11:10.790 --> 00:11:16.910
Good idea. Killing a tian outside of war
gets you on the wanted list, after all.

00:11:16.910 --> 00:11:20.950
Oh, right--could you tweak your setting a bit?

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:22.410
In what way?

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:25.080
Ray Starling goes through.

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:27.450
Why?

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:31.830
Because I'm going to fight him, duh.

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:33.040
Got it, si--

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:36.870
In here, you call me "Leader," Yu.

00:11:38.330 --> 00:11:40.950
Yes, Leader.

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:55.790
Another fine spectacle!

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:58.330
You must be Franklin.

00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:01.250
The one and only, in the flesh!

00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:04.370
We are taking back Her Highness Elizabeth.

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:06.660
Now <i>that's</i> a problem.

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:09.790
Then we'll do so by force.

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:11.870
You can attack me?

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:19.870
Fear not. We of the Royal Guard are bound by
magic that prevents us from harming royalty.

00:12:19.870 --> 00:12:23.200
Wow! I'm kinda jealous.

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:27.330
But it pains me to turn my
blade against the princess,

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:30.080
so I would appreciate your letting her go.

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:34.040
Screw <i>that</i> !

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:37.200
Grand Cross!

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:53.200
That was close. Good thing
I had that Lifesaving Brooch.

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:56.080
That Superior Killer...

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:58.790
I'm really piling on the ol' expenses today.

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:00.660
Charge!

00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:07.290
How convenient--right when I wanted
to take this baby out for a test drive.

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:10.200
Call: RSK!

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:24.790
I, Yuri Gautier, was born into an upper-class
family in the south of France.

00:13:24.790 --> 00:13:29.540
My father was a wealthy man
who'd made a fortune in his lifetime.

00:13:29.540 --> 00:13:35.660
My mother, once an actress on the stage,
was beautiful and kind.

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:41.080
I would brag about my much-older sister,
gifted with both good looks and brains.

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:45.700
Seen from the outside, we may well
have been a family to be envied,

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:49.450
but from my inside perspective,
things were quite different.

00:13:49.450 --> 00:13:53.750
My father was domineering
and took it out on my mother.

00:13:53.750 --> 00:14:00.160
My mother bore it all with nary a
harsh word or action toward us girls.

00:14:00.160 --> 00:14:08.080
My sister, though always kind to me,
seemed to have worries of her own.

00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:12.120
One day, after our pet iguana died,
our grandfather made a plaster likeness of it

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:15.370
for my grieving sister.

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:19.080
That led to her learning the
craft from our grandfather

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:22.910
and making plaster animals of her own.

00:14:22.910 --> 00:14:25.250
How long can you keep doing this?

00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:28.250
Your future husband has already
been chosen for you--

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:31.370
he'll never love you if you stink of plaster!

00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:35.950
And so my sister left.

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:40.450
My mother and father blamed
each other for her leaving,

00:14:40.450 --> 00:14:44.500
and reached the obvious conclusion: Divorce.

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:49.160
I had only one thought
during these early years...

00:14:49.160 --> 00:14:52.830
...that I should have protected them better.

00:14:52.830 --> 00:14:57.910
Both my mother... and my sister.

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:07.540
If I'd kept them safe from their tormentor,
this never would have happened.

00:15:07.540 --> 00:15:13.080
If I could have been like a knight in the plays
my mother used to take me to,

00:15:13.080 --> 00:15:18.500
a strong man who could have protected them...

00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:24.000
But I understood this fervent wish
was one that would never be granted.

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:28.160
Then, half a year after my parents' divorce,

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:32.290
I came across a world that could
make that wish come true.

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:35.660
" <i>Infinite Dendrogram</i> offers a new world
and your own unique possibilities."

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:42.000
I wanted Hugo to be the embodiment
of my childhood wish,

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:47.000
a knight that would defeat any tragedies
that threaten helpless women.

00:15:48.830 --> 00:15:51.000
Hugo, are you all right?

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:53.330
Yes, fine.

00:15:53.330 --> 00:15:56.790
If you're fretting this much, we can still quit.

00:15:56.790 --> 00:15:58.870
No...

00:15:58.870 --> 00:16:03.290
This way will be far less
damaging in the long term.

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:08.790
If we make the kingdom surrender now,
we can avoid a pointless war.

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:12.620
Besides, we're only targeting Masters.

00:16:12.620 --> 00:16:15.250
It seems so hard on you.

00:16:15.250 --> 00:16:17.910
Thanks for your concern.

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:23.910
But--and this is personal on
my part--I want to help him.

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:26.750
I'll be with you, Hugo.

00:16:28.660 --> 00:16:30.580
Thanks.

00:16:30.580 --> 00:16:34.870
I'm renouncing the role that Hugo's been given.

00:16:35.830 --> 00:16:38.040
You came, Ray.

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:45.450
"No Master shall pass beyond this point."

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:49.330
Do you want me here or not, Hugo?

00:16:49.330 --> 00:16:52.080
I'm not sure myself.

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:54.000
Where's Franklin?

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:58.750
Beyond this gate, battling the
Knights of the Royal Guard.

00:16:58.750 --> 00:17:01.540
Then we're going through, too.

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:06.410
You're free to pass, but I can't
let your friends through.

00:17:06.410 --> 00:17:08.160
Why just me?

00:17:08.160 --> 00:17:11.950
The boss wants to fight you himself.

00:17:11.950 --> 00:17:15.580
Franklin does? What for?

00:17:18.580 --> 00:17:21.000
You go on ahead, Ray.

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:26.830
You've got enough to worry about
on both sides of the gate.

00:17:26.830 --> 00:17:33.410
Hurry on through. I'll take care
of this end in your place.

00:17:33.410 --> 00:17:37.660
I know this is a friend of yours
who fought at your side yesterday.

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:39.870
Which is why I can say this:

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:43.410
If you don't make it in time, you'll regret it.

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:46.910
So you'd better get a move on, Ray.

00:17:46.910 --> 00:17:50.660
Thanks, Rook. He's all yours.

00:17:50.660 --> 00:17:52.410
I got this!

00:17:56.910 --> 00:17:58.040
Hugo!

00:17:58.040 --> 00:18:01.540
I apologize for going back on my word, Ray,

00:18:01.540 --> 00:18:04.410
but would you join me in a single
exchange of all-out blows?

00:18:04.410 --> 00:18:08.540
Sure. There's a lot I want to ask
and a lot I want to say,

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:11.370
but right now, let's go with one attack each!

00:18:11.370 --> 00:18:12.950
<i>Merci.</i>

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:15.750
Motor Slash!

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:20.040
Counter Absorption!

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:25.410
Vengeance is Mine!

00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:31.450
So he used it.

00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:40.370
Using Counter Absorption now leaves Ray with
shackles he can't ignore in the fight to come.

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:48.540
Seriously... why am I so...? How could I--?

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:51.290
For you, that was--

00:18:55.580 --> 00:18:59.040
Sorry. You were wide open.

00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:04.540
Little Flare!

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:06.620
You coward.

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:12.200
That's uncalled for. I told you, didn't I?
That I'd take care of this end?

00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:16.160
It's not my fault you were lost in thought.

00:19:16.160 --> 00:19:20.540
For someone who's Ray's friend,
you're nothing like him.

00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:25.700
Maybe so. Maybe that's why I admire him so much.

00:19:25.700 --> 00:19:29.660
Also, I think I hate you.

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:33.580
That's the first time you've
ever said you hated anyone!

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:37.620
So it's hate at first sight, huh?

00:19:37.620 --> 00:19:41.790
That's right. But you really are loathsome.

00:19:41.790 --> 00:19:47.200
You're so indecisive, so uppity--
like a certain someone.

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:49.790
You're talking nonsense.

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:51.950
Am I, though?

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:54.450
I haven't the slightest idea what you mean.

00:19:54.450 --> 00:19:59.410
Regardless, I'll freeze you where you stand!

00:20:01.910 --> 00:20:04.250
I cannot let you pass.

00:20:04.250 --> 00:20:10.040
As a member of the Triangle of Wisdom...
and as the thorn that protects him.

00:20:10.040 --> 00:20:17.660
I see. Then I'll defeat you with all
I have and force my way through.

00:20:17.660 --> 00:20:22.830
As Ray's friend--and as myself.

00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:28.120
High Pilot Hugo Lesseps and his Embryo, Cocytus!

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:35.160
Pimp Rook Holmes, his Embryo, Babylon,
and his tamed beasts Marilyn and Audrey!

00:20:35.160 --> 00:20:37.660
Now we fight...

00:20:37.660 --> 00:20:39.790
...fair and square!

00:20:39.790 --> 00:20:41.910
The test went well.

00:20:41.910 --> 00:20:46.410
Its attacks were a little on the
weak side, but what can you do?

00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:48.950
Sir Lindos! We'll use the stack!

00:20:55.290 --> 00:20:57.200
--Grand Cross!
--Grand Cross!

00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:05.200
Not bad, not bad at all.
Completely pointless, though.

00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:11.870
Impossible! The stack had no effect?!

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:16.080
If only you hadn't been Paladins with
your Holy element and your swords,

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:18.750
you might have actually stood a chance.

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:21.700
After all, this RSK here...

00:21:25.660 --> 00:21:28.870
He's here! He's here, he's here, he's here!

00:21:28.870 --> 00:21:30.620
Here he is!

00:21:31.830 --> 00:21:34.120
Ray?! What are <i>you</i> doing here?

00:21:34.120 --> 00:21:38.830
This whole abducting-children thing
leaves a bad taste in my mouth.

00:21:38.830 --> 00:21:42.950
And I figured I'd crush <i>him</i> ,
too, while I'm at it!

00:21:44.120 --> 00:21:47.080
Excellent--truly excellent!

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:53.620
You don't often see people as earnest
as you here in <i>Infinite Dendrogram</i> .

00:21:53.620 --> 00:21:56.290
It'll be <i>so</i> worth it to snap you in two!

00:21:56.290 --> 00:22:02.200
You'll pay, Flamingo--for today
<i>and</i> for what you did yesterday!

00:22:04.120 --> 00:22:10.410
Then I'll have <i>you</i> pay for what
